course: dictionary
lesson: 570
title: Dancing lights in the sky
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: You can often work out a word from the words around it. This is called context. In «Jupiter has the most powerful auroras in the Solar System, glowing at its poles in ultraviolet light», the clues are glowing, poles and light. So an aurora must be a kind of light that glows, not a mountain or an animal.
explain: Read on to find more clues. «The Earth's magnetic field shields us from most of the solar wind, and particles leaking in near the poles make the aurora.» The particles near the poles make the aurora, so an aurora comes from tiny particles hitting the air. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence to check it makes sense.
explain: Be careful with capital letters. Aurora with a capital A can be a girl's name, the Roman goddess of the dawn, or the name of Sleeping Beauty in a Disney film. Look at the sentence: if it talks about light in the sky, it means the lights. If it talks about a person, it is a name.
fact: An aurora is a display of moving, coloured light, often green, pink or purple, in the night sky.
fact: Auroras are seen near the North or South Pole: the aurora borealis (northern lights) and the aurora australis (southern lights).
fact: Auroras happen when tiny charged particles from the Sun hit gases high in Earth's atmosphere and make them glow.
fact: Earth's magnetic field steers those particles towards the poles.
fact: People travel to Norway, Iceland, Canada, Scotland, Tasmania and New Zealand to see the lights.
exercise: «Jupiter has the most powerful auroras in the Solar System, glowing at its poles in ultraviolet light.» What is an aurora in this sentence? | A girl's name | *A display of moving, glowing light in the sky | A tall mountain on Jupiter | A type of fish that lives in the sea
exercise: What other name is the aurora borealis known by? | Ultraviolet light | The southern lights | The solar wind | *The northern lights
exercise: In «Aurora was the first to wake up that morning», what kind of word is Aurora? | A kind of gas | *A name | A type of light | A place on a map
test: «Near solar maximum, as in 2024, aurorae were seen much further from the poles than usual, even in England.» What is the plural of aurora used here? | auroras only | aurora-s | *aurorae | aurorum
test: What makes the particles in an aurora travel towards the poles? | Sea waves | The moon's gravity only | The Sun's heat alone | *Earth's magnetic field
exam: Which phrase means the southern lights? | solar wind | aurora goddess | *aurora australis | aurora borealis
